INSERT INTO schema_problem.problem_solution OVERRIDING SYSTEM VALUE VALUES (406, 112, 'Optimized Java Solution', '#  Intuition

At each gas station, if the amount of gas is greater than or equal to the cost to reach the next station, you can continue the journey. The core idea is to determine if there''s a starting station from which you can complete the entire circuit by calculating the remaining gas after each stop.


# Approach

- Compute the difference gas[i] - cost[i] for each station and store it in the diff array.

- Calculate the total sum of all differences. If the sum is less than 0, it means there''s not enough gas to complete the circuit → return -1.

- Traverse the diff array:

- Accumulate the value to from start to end.

- If at any point to < 0, it means the current segment cannot reach the next station → update the starting index to i + 1 and reset to = 0.

- After the loop, the index will point to the first station from which a complete circuit is possible.

# Complexity

## Time complexity:

O(n) — The array is traversed twice: once for summation and once for finding the valid starting index.

## Space complexity:

O(n) — Due to the use of the diff array which has the same size as the input.
 # Code 
