If you want to remove a selected code, click the ''X'' icon in the button have id that you want to removed. 
You cannot delete or edit the selected code here. 
Please choose at least one code.
-->', false, 1, '2025-04-27 20:41:12.602844', 1, '2025-04-27 20:42:22.325494', 1, 0);
INSERT INTO schema_problem.problem_solution OVERRIDING SYSTEM VALUE VALUES (410, 112, 'Kodeholik - Editorial', '## Intuition:
The problem requires finding the starting gas station from which a car can complete a circuit. At each station, we gain some gas and need to spend some to reach the next. If the total gas is less than the total cost, completing the circuit is impossible. Otherwise, there must exist a starting point that allows us to complete the trip without ever running out of gas.

## Approach:

First, calculate the net gas gain (gas[i] - cost[i]) at each station and sum it up across all stations. If the total is negative, we immediately return -1 because there is not enough gas to complete the circuit. Otherwise, we scan through the stations, tracking the cumulative gas balance. If the balance ever drops below zero, it means we cannot reach the next station from the current start point, so we reset the balance and set the starting station to the next one.

## Complexity:

- **Time Complexity:** O(n), where n is the number of stations, since we traverse the array twice at most.

- **Space Complexity:** O(n), due to the auxiliary array diff used to store gas-cost differences.', true, 0, '2025-04-28 08:29:00.212673', 22, NULL, NULL, 0);
